<section id="why">
  <div class="container">
    
    <div class="section-label">Architecture Decision Record</div>
    <h2>Why the ADR arrived late — and what that teaches</h2>

    <p style="color:var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; max-width: 640px;">
      The huhuGERMAN ADR was written <em>after</em> the MVP, not before. That honesty is deliberate.
      A system that documents its decisions retroactively understands something a system
      that never documents them never will.
    </p>

    <div class="adr-timeline">
      <div class="adr-entry">
        <div class="adr-date">2011 — Origin</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Observation begins at FCPyS-UNAM</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          First longitudinal observation of the Hochdeutsch/Umgangssprache gap in Mexican students.
          Authentic input introduced informally. The method precedes the theory — 
          formalized later in the B.A. thesis (2015) and M.Ed. thesis (2020).
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="adr-entry">
        <div class="adr-date">2022 — MVP</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Endpoint + AI + implicit context</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          Validated the flow: student submits → AI gives feedback. Proved the pedagogical
          hypothesis was worth building. But context lived in the teacher's head, not the system.
          The AI corrected Perfekt for students in week 2. System not yet governable.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="adr-entry">
        <div class="adr-date">2024 — Friction Discovery</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Domain-level misalignment surfaces</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          Students reported confusion from feedback on grammar they hadn't seen.
          This was not a bug. It was a missing domain contract.
          "When a system depends on human judgment to not break, it's not a product."
          Documented classroom friction — now research data for the article.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="adr-entry">
        <div class="adr-date">2025 — ADR Written</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Pedagogical domain as typed source of truth</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          WochenKontextSchema formalizes gelernt / nicht_gelernt / korrektur.
          prompt-builder constructs prompts from domain. AI obeys, not decides.
          Zod validates at every boundary. JSONB snapshots enable research audit trail.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="adr-entry dim">
        <div class="adr-date">May 2026 — Publication</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Targeting Die Unterrichtspraxis (AATG · Q3 ESCI)</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          The system becomes evidence for the research trajectory:
          B.A. thesis (2015) as theoretical foundation, M.Ed. thesis (2020) as diagnostic phase,
          huhuGERMAN as intervention. First editorial milestone in a planned sequence.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-label" style="margin-top: 5rem;">Pedagogical Decision Record</div>
    <h2 id="pdr">PDR: Governing the AI, not just building it</h2>

    <p style="color:var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; max-width: 640px;">
      If an AI doesn't know the "State of the Classroom," it shouldn't generate a single line of content. 
      The PDR is a hard-coded contract — ensuring pedagogy governs technology, not the other way around.
    </p>

    <div class="adr-timeline">
      <div class="adr-entry">
        <div class="adr-date">The Contract</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Pedagogical Domain as Typed Truth</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          huhuGERMAN formalizes the WochenKontext (Weekly Context). No generic LLM magic.
          If a concept is marked as nicht_gelernt in the PDR, 
          the system is architecturally forbidden from generating feedback on it.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="adr-entry">
        <div class="adr-date">The Governance</div>
        <div class="adr-title">PDR as System Prompt</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          Every prompt is wrapped in a PDR snapshot. 
          The AI obeys the boundary constraints defined by the educator. 
          The error is not a bug — it's a boundary condition.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="adr-entry dim">
        <div class="adr-date">RFC-001</div>
        <div class="adr-title">Standardizing Pedagogy</div>
        <div class="adr-desc">
          Moving from "I hope the AI gets it right" to "The system cannot generate it wrong."
          The PDR structure is being documented as part of the research publication trajectory.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>